WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.500
Sometimes we don't know our own strength.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.660
It can be hard to tell just how much weight you can safely bear

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.380
or how much will crush you.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.290
I'd like to think you can shoulder as big a burden as you believe you can,

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.170
that it's all a matter of will.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.060
Certainly a comforting thought.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.360
In a way not three months,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.280
the girl accumulates a lifetime's worth of possessions.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.230
Tell her there just is not room enough for this much refuse.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:29.910
Maybe not now.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.340
Perhaps not.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.380
Well, drive it.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.960
Been a hell of a ride.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.000
Grab it.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.220
If you make me cry.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.490
None of that for me, little girl.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.810
Oh, come on, Irv.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.950
You know you're going to miss me.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.660
I'm serious about the TiVo.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.000
You can't be a VCR man forever.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.880
All right, this is it.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:13.030
I don't expect you to forgive me or even like me.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.110
I'm hoping you can at least accept a thank you.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:18.640
You saved my life.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.520
Actually, it's my daughter who saved your life.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.150
All I did was show up.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:34.820
It's been two days.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.420
Didn't you want to make sure I was okay?

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:38.890
I called the hospital.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.270
They said you were released yesterday.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.920
So are you going to leave a forwarding address

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.580
or just going for a clean getaway?

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:46.980
I'm just going home.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:48.860
Good.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:49.280
Yeah.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.990
I'll give you a call later.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.230
Let you get settled then.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.250
No, don't.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.520
I think we both know that we can't keep doing this, Tommy.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:01:59.960
Okay.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.820
Look, Amy, I screwed up. I know that.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.380
I never should have taken you to that party,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.500
and we never should have done all that crap,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.940
but this whole thing has been such a serious wake-up call for me.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.750
I'm glad. I hope that you get the help that you need.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.180
Amy, I don't need help. I just need you.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.400
I can't be that person for you anymore, Tommy.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.940
It was just a slip. One slip, one night.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:24.900
That's not who I am.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.940
It wasn't one night. It was three months of lies.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.900
So what? I'm not good enough for you anymore?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.120
Are you going to go back to mommy and daddy?

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.320
Going to go back to being Little Miss Perfect, is that it?

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.600
Well, you can't.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:43.700
You won't be able to, not after us.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:47.460
You got to go.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.080
Take care of yourself, Tommy.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.400
Other times, it's hard to remember you had any strength

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:55.800
at all.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.980
Then you can only hope to have someone to remind you.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.660
You were once fierce and able.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:05.600
Are you okay?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:06.470
Yeah.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:08.970
Go home.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.930
Like I told you, you got to throw it really hard.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:27.910
He's late, Andy.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:29.920
Only five.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.850
minutes. You doing okay?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.500
Maybe he's not coming. Maybe he changes

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.340
his mind about the whole thing. Do you think? I mean,

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.680
it's possible. I gotta go to the bathroom.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:40.600
Stay. I'll take it.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:55.080
Hi. Hi. You look good, Nina.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.240
Thanks. Thank you.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.280
So is that it? Is that all we're going to do? You have nothing else to say to me?

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.300
Come on, don't. It's hard enough.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.740
You have no idea how hard it is.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.060
Dad's here!

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.600
Hey, look at you. You've grown a whole foot.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.140
Dr. Brown, nice to see you.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:15.920
Hello, Carl.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:20.510
His toothbrush is in the pouch, but the game starts at 9, they said...

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.940
See you there at 8.30. I know.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.380
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.100
So she hasn't actually said the words.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:34.920
She doesn't need to.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.240
I can tell by the way she looked at me.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.160
Go away, little man.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.780
Come back when you're older or taller or just somebody else.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.640
She has very expressive eyes.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.200
This is good.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.200
So, you know, you're still holding some cards.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.340
What cards?

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.140
I have no cards.

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:50.330
You could break up with her first.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.370
I mean, sure, you're going to miss out on a lot of pity sex,

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.960
but sometimes your pride comes before your nads.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:57.570
Not very often, but it happens.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.910
I think you're missing the point here.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.870
I don't want to break up with her.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.950
I'm trying to preserve a relationship with Madison.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.430
Yeah, and if that was a possibility, you'd be over there right now with hand on boob.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.730
You really don't think I can fix things?

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:11.010
You tackled her guitarist, got kicked out of the first club that ever gave her a paying gig.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.860
I don't think God could fix this.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:21.160
See you later.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.300
Can't keep avoiding me, Bright.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.000
Our rooms are like two feet away from each other.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.110
He was using my room as his own personal gym.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:37.810
Can you believe that?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:38.780
No comment.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.210
Yeah, sorry, not your problem.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:42.810
It's just been a really crappy day.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.920
I'm sure it must be weird coming home after all this time,

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.170
but everything will get back to normal soon enough.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.100
That's one way to look at it.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.420
Tommy had a slightly different take on the whole thing.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.760
I'm sure he had a good point in his own special way.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.300
Broke up this morning.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:06:59.740
He did?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:03.980
Are you okay?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.180
Yeah, I think so.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:11.700
Kind of saw it coming, you know, like we were forcing things and then that whole thing happened.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.940
I'm sure that you heard.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.880
Yeah, I think pretty much everybody heard.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:17.920
It sounded pretty scary.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:24.130
It's okay.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:24.970
It's for the best.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.410
How are things with you?

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.430
A little Madison thing.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.180
Good.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:29.780
Good.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.520
I mean, you know, she's been real busy with the band and stuff.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.000
But other than that, it's been really good.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:34.580
Oh, good.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:41.150
Well, it's good to know that one of us made a relationship work this year.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:43.900
Can I, uh...

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:44.850
Okay.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:45.620
Sure.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.760
So I take it the fun zone wasn't so fun?

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:58.540
Nope.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:07:59.960
Fun zone was definitely not...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.980
It's not a fun zone.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.600
I've never seen Nina so nervous.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.250
I knew he was up to something.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.610
I could tell from the way he was acting this morning,

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.070
but I never.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:09.980
I'm going to kill him, Andy.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.320
I swear to God, I am going to kill him.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:12.700
What happened?

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.020
He's asking for sole custody of Sam.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:16.110
What?

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:17.910
Can't do that.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:19.930
That's what I said, but apparently he can.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.470
He got a promotion last month.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:22.550
He's making tons of cash.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:23.770
I can't compete with that.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.460
Plus, he's enrolled Sam in some fancy private school.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:28.240
I wasn't even going to ask for alimony.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:28.980
I'm such an idiot.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.340
I'm gonna lose Sam, aren't I?

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.080
No, you're not.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.830
You know, there's a lot more to parenting than how much money you make,

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.190
and one visit isn't gonna make up for all of his neglect.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.560
Kids are smart. They can see through all that.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:43.370
Yeah, and the course may be changing,

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.710
but this is still a small, conservative county.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.510
The odds of any judge giving sole custody to a single gay father,

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.630
I mean, it's a long shot.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.830
You don't need to worry, I'm telling you.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.090
She's right, Nina. No one's gonna take Sam away from you.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.570
You're gonna win this case.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:03.760
Hey.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:09.650
Hey.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:21.130
Still working on a little anger right now.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.110
You're going to have to give me a second.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.070
Yeah, take your time.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.780
Freezing my ass off outside a police station

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.880
was definitely not as cool as getting

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.770
My band signed by a manager wasn't exactly the way I thought the night would go, you know?

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.260
I know. I'm sorry.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.660
You know, what really made me mad, though, is when you didn't call. You said you would call.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.250
Well, I didn't think you really wanted me to. I thought you were just saying that to be nice.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.900
We thought wrong. I wanted you to call so that we could talk, you know?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.420
It's one of the things I like about us, Ephraim.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.440
We don't play games. You tell me how you feel. I know exactly where we stand.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.450
That's my problem. I say too much. No filter.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:09:59.980
You should have...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.380
If I knew that not calling is the reason

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.560
you were going to break up with me.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:06.860
Who said I'm breaking up with you?

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:07.910
You did.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:08.630
The other day, you.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:13.250
I'm just going to stop talking now.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.730
Look, I'm not going to lie to you.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:20.090
This relationship is hard, maybe a little harder than most.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.010
But so what?

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:24.180
That's the way relationships get, right?

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:24.980
That's how they are.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.780
Yeah, I guess.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.630
So we work on it.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.970
I mean, how pathetic are we if we just

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.820
bail at the first sign of trouble.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:32.860
It's not me.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.540
I know it's not you.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:35.660
No, not at all.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:36.760
Me neither.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.100
At least I don't want it to be me.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.730
Maybe it has been me in the past.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.350
There's good stuff here.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.850
There's stuff that I think is worth saving.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:59.470
What I mean is, I know that we have things to work out,

00:10:59.590 --> 00:10:59.970
but I'm not.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.540
to try if you are?

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.160
Yeah.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.120
I think that trying is definitely the right thing to do here.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.500
I think that's much better than that other not trying thing.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.420
I think that's bad.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.220
OK, good.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:12.900
This is good.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:13.920
This is great.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.680
So we'll just back it up a couple of notches, regroup,

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:17.780
maintain hope.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.960
Remain cautiously optimistic.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:26.640
A little hint for you, though.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.760
If you forget my birthday, it's over.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:29.890
Oh, you got a birthday?

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:43.580
funny laughing Brad and Eric are definitely coming tonight we can offer

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:49.290
in my car but we might have to sit on the laps I'll take Eric's lap where are

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:56.980
you guys going okay they just opened this drive-in diner where the deli used

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.690
to be can be the place to be from now on

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.710
Yeah, um, I heard about that. So you guys are all going?

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:04.080
It's like fun.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.540
What are you doing here?

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:11.290
I was thinking about joining class again, but I don't know if Mrs. Baxworth will...

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:15.230
We heard you, like, OD'd and had to go to the emergency room and get your stomach pumped.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:16.880
That is so gross.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.490
It didn't exactly happen. See?

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:21.330
No track marks.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.440
Are you really going out with Tommy Callahan?

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.080
No, we broke up, actually.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:29.970
Are we supposed to be sad for you?

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:36.940
No, I was just telling you, in case you're wondering or curious or whatever.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:37.940
We weren't.

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.090
Oh, so it is true.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.820
Someone wrote Amy Abbott on the class roll, and I thought it was a joke.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.200
Welcome back, sweetie.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.490
Oh, don't know where you've been, but it must have treated you well.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.010
You're just skinny as a twig.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.320
All right, everyone, on your feet.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:57.980
I want to see plies, and I want to see them now.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:12:59.930
And bye.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:05.210
five, six, seven, eight, turn up your hips and nod your feet.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:10.950
When I finally came out, it was like this huge burden lifting.

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:13.990
Like everything had been cloudy and all of a sudden I could see.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.120
Felt better physically, I started connecting with people again.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:22.300
I wasn't ashamed or afraid, and I don't know,

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:23.720
I guess I got my confidence back.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:25.580
That's when I got the job.

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.930
And how long have you been employed at Carnahan Systems?

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.250
Just under a year.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.340
bought the house last month when they made me vice president. And your salary is $120,000 a year,

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:41.710
correct? Plus pension and health. Sam's on the policy, also on my life insurance. I started a

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:46.340
college fund last year, and I've already got a place for him at Lamplighter, which is right by

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:56.500
my house. Thank you. Your witness. Mr. Feeney, what's your son's favorite book? Well, there's

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.880
probably more than one. Sam loves to read.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.660
Can you tell me the name of his teacher?

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.250
Again, he's got a lot of them.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.300
So pick one.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:11.370
Tell me the name of just one of the teachers who spends time educating your son.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.030
I, uh, can't recall.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:19.750
You don't know anything about Sam's life, do you, sir?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.450
Ever since you walked out on him over a year ago.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:29.540
Look, maybe I can't sit here right now and tell you every detail about Sam's day-to-day life, but...

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.330
That's what this is all about.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.700
I want to be a part of it again.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:38.800
I want to be there when he wakes up, when he comes home from school, to tuck him in at night.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.330
I've already missed too much.

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:43.010
I just want to share everything with him.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:44.780
Have you shared the fact that you're gay?

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:45.940
Your Honor, this is redundant.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:47.520
We already know about Mr. Feeney.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.220
We know.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.560
That wasn't the question I was asking about Sam.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.000
Besides, I believe he opened the door.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.760
I'll ask you again, Mr. Feeney.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:57.570
