00:30:38.840 --> 00:30:42.580
But she's already made plans to move to Denver in case she loses today.

00:30:42.880 --> 00:30:44.460
To be near her son.

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:47.740
And I hope she doesn't have to do that.

00:30:50.770 --> 00:30:54.780
Your Honor, I know you're here to determine the best interests of this child.

00:30:55.880 --> 00:30:59.120
And I know it falls outside of my jurisdiction as a doctor.

00:30:59.200 --> 00:30:59.980
But I have to tell you...

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:06.220
you that it is in the best interests of anyone to live in Nina's company and be a part of her

00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:18.060
life. Please, please don't take her and Sam away from us. We need her here. I need her. Of course,

00:31:18.060 --> 00:31:22.900
we're going to object to all that. It's not in response to the question. There even was a question.

00:31:24.360 --> 00:31:24.740
Overruled.

00:31:36.170 --> 00:31:42.960
I thought you were at dance class.

00:31:43.230 --> 00:31:43.870
I'm not going.

00:31:46.190 --> 00:31:48.150
Right, I'm tired, and I just want to go home, okay?

00:31:48.370 --> 00:31:48.990
No, you don't.

00:31:49.130 --> 00:31:51.210
You want to go to class, but you're scared.

00:31:51.490 --> 00:31:52.190
I'm not scared.

00:31:54.030 --> 00:31:54.490
I'm not.

00:31:54.790 --> 00:31:56.500
Look, it's your life.

00:31:56.910 --> 00:31:58.530
You get to decide what to do with it, not them.

00:32:02.010 --> 00:32:02.770
I can't go in there.

00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:04.520
Yeah, you can.

00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:07.840
You're the best dancer in the school.

00:32:08.390 --> 00:32:11.330
You shouldn't just give up what you love because some asshats made you feel bad.

00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:13.060
Screw them.

00:32:13.240 --> 00:32:13.760
They'll come around.

00:32:14.120 --> 00:32:14.740
How do you know?

00:32:14.740 --> 00:32:15.440
You haven't.

00:32:16.030 --> 00:32:16.950
You were there the other night.

00:32:17.010 --> 00:32:17.710
You saw what they did.

00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:18.890
You didn't do anything about it.

00:32:19.340 --> 00:32:20.580
That's because I was still mad.

00:32:21.780 --> 00:32:24.170
If you want to know the truth, I'm still a little pissed off.

00:32:24.290 --> 00:32:26.210
You seriously messed up my senior year.

00:32:26.470 --> 00:32:27.670
Which only happens once.

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:29.960
Or like...

00:32:30.120 --> 00:32:30.380
Twice.

00:32:30.560 --> 00:32:32.320
If you're still mad, then why do you even care?

00:32:33.780 --> 00:32:34.140
Because.

00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:36.920
It was messed up what Paige did to you.

00:32:37.880 --> 00:32:44.240
I don't like seeing you being treated that way, you know?

00:32:45.210 --> 00:32:46.670
I mean, I can treat you like that,

00:32:46.730 --> 00:32:49.710
but if everyone else starts doing it, where's the fun in that?

00:32:52.570 --> 00:32:53.590
Don't get over it, Amy.

00:32:54.290 --> 00:32:56.320
Just, you gotta stay in their face about it, okay?

00:32:57.500 --> 00:32:58.280
Gotta be you.

00:33:00.640 --> 00:33:03.930
Oh, be yourself.

00:33:05.800 --> 00:33:09.070
Annoying, self-righteous, pain in the ass.

00:33:09.310 --> 00:33:09.550
You.

00:33:09.790 --> 00:33:10.770
Keep talking, brother.

00:33:11.010 --> 00:33:11.890
Keep talking.

00:33:22.420 --> 00:33:23.140
Open up without you.

00:33:25.800 --> 00:33:26.900
Sorry, I just had to go.

00:33:31.980 --> 00:33:33.500
You're not the one who should be sorry, it's me.

00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:37.440
I shouldn't have gotten so drunk.

00:33:37.600 --> 00:33:40.100
I didn't realize I was...

00:33:40.410 --> 00:33:41.230
Are you kidding me?

00:33:42.310 --> 00:33:43.690
It was your 21st birthday.

00:33:43.850 --> 00:33:44.350
I think it's a lot.

00:33:44.450 --> 00:33:46.060
In fact, I think it's mandatory.

00:33:55.920 --> 00:33:56.620
First, or should I?

00:33:57.950 --> 00:33:58.370
I will.

00:34:18.010 --> 00:34:19.150
Well, at least we tried.

00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:22.600
And at the end of the day, we really tried.

00:34:25.150 --> 00:34:29.970
Right now, I wish that there was something that I can.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:36.940
could change it we could change I mean if there was anything that we could

00:34:36.940 --> 00:34:41.730
actually do to save this thing I'd do that in a heartbeat you know that right

00:34:42.680 --> 00:34:53.310
if only my parents had had sex four years earlier you're the most amazing guy

00:34:54.590 --> 00:34:56.680
Please, don't do that, please.

00:34:56.840 --> 00:34:59.010
You have to.

00:35:01.820 --> 00:35:05.890
There's a part of me that did fall, really, truly fall.

00:35:06.050 --> 00:35:13.500
I know you didn't feel it, and I'm sorry that you didn't,

00:35:13.560 --> 00:35:22.080
but it was there, and I need you to know that and believe it.

00:35:36.690 --> 00:35:41.740
I know that if I open this, it's going to be perfect.

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.360
It's just going to make me sadder,

00:35:43.420 --> 00:35:52.770
because you're so perfect, so I can't.

00:36:00.160 --> 00:36:00.900
Delia or should I?

00:36:04.180 --> 00:36:04.540
Delia.

00:36:04.740 --> 00:36:06.940
No, I can tell her if you want me to.

00:36:07.200 --> 00:36:07.830
It doesn't matter.

00:36:10.240 --> 00:36:10.560
I'll do it.

00:36:11.280 --> 00:36:14.850
I'll come by later or tomorrow, maybe.

00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:16.620
Figure out what to say.

00:36:17.070 --> 00:36:28.780
Here we go.

00:36:52.200 --> 00:36:52.820
Please be seated.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:05.990
matter of Feeney versus Feeney, the court has made its decision. Having considered the pleadings,

00:37:06.110 --> 00:37:11.240
evidence, and arguments of counsel, the court is of the opinion that it's in the best interests of

00:37:11.240 --> 00:37:17.770
the minor child, Samuel David Feeney, that respondent Margaret Nina Feeney be designated

00:37:17.770 --> 00:37:24.400
primary care parent subject to a reasonable and standard parenting time awarded to petitioner

00:37:25.160 --> 00:37:27.020
and determined at a future date.

00:37:31.240 --> 00:37:32.440
Your son is staying with you.

00:37:37.180 --> 00:37:37.880
Thank you, counsel.

00:38:09.560 --> 00:38:10.880
Congratulations, you win.

00:38:12.320 --> 00:38:14.000
I never wanted this fight to begin with.

00:38:15.520 --> 00:38:16.940
Look, we don't have to argue anymore.

00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:18.840
We don't even have to talk if that's what you want.

00:38:19.390 --> 00:38:20.630
That's not what I want, Nina.

00:38:21.290 --> 00:38:22.610
I never meant to be your enemy.

00:38:22.610 --> 00:38:24.070
I just wanted to be with Sam again.

00:38:24.350 --> 00:38:26.190
I offered you that, and you wanted more.

00:38:26.690 --> 00:38:28.880
I know, and I'm sorry.

00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:29.980
I thought I would...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.740
doing the right thing i really did and yesterday when andy was talking about the accident i was

00:38:34.740 --> 00:38:40.830
so happy i thought i could win i didn't even think about what you went through that night

00:38:40.830 --> 00:38:47.300
or what sam went through i was just happy you made a mistake that's when i realized

00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:58.950
i wasn't thinking about who the better parent was this whole time i just missed him you missed it

00:39:00.030 --> 00:39:01.450
Tell Sam I'm happy for him.

00:39:01.600 --> 00:39:02.300
Tell him yourself.

00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:03.400
Yeah, this weekend.

00:39:14.320 --> 00:39:14.880
You heard about Nina?

00:39:15.800 --> 00:39:17.080
Just going next door to celebrate.

00:39:17.340 --> 00:39:17.860
Want to come over?

00:39:18.200 --> 00:39:20.120
Do you really think I've become such a bad father

00:39:20.120 --> 00:39:20.960
that I wouldn't find out?

00:39:22.090 --> 00:39:22.690
Find out what?

00:39:22.890 --> 00:39:24.570
You gave Amy birth control pills.

00:39:24.830 --> 00:39:26.510
I'd like you to tell me what the hell you were thinking.

00:39:28.070 --> 00:39:28.990
She came to me.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.200
We discussed it. I couldn't just send her away.

00:39:32.380 --> 00:39:33.780
That's exactly what you should have done.

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:36.500
If I had done that, she would have just gone to someone else.

00:39:36.780 --> 00:39:40.460
I thought she'd rather she at least have someone who would look after her, talk to her.

00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:42.600
You have no idea what I would rather.

00:39:43.040 --> 00:39:44.480
How could you not come to me?

00:39:44.700 --> 00:39:47.540
I don't know what to say. She asked me specifically not to tell you.

00:39:47.780 --> 00:39:49.660
Of course she did. She wouldn't have come to you in the first place

00:39:49.660 --> 00:39:51.260
if she didn't think she was doing something wrong.

00:39:51.480 --> 00:39:53.120
She wasn't doing anything wrong.

00:39:53.340 --> 00:39:55.700
She made a responsible decision, the right one for her.

00:39:56.460 --> 00:39:57.600
She thought it through carefully.

00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:59.580
She considered her reasons and her options.

00:40:00.990 --> 00:40:02.450
You raised a very smart young woman.

00:40:02.570 --> 00:40:03.250
She's not a woman.

00:40:03.570 --> 00:40:04.110
To you, she's not.

00:40:04.110 --> 00:40:05.110
She is 16.

00:40:05.780 --> 00:40:06.140
16.

00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:08.080
You know the law as well as I do.

00:40:08.220 --> 00:40:09.640
She merits confidentiality.

00:40:10.040 --> 00:40:11.460
As a doctor, I had no choice.

00:40:11.460 --> 00:40:13.720
I have no interest in your thoughts as a doctor.

00:40:13.840 --> 00:40:15.220
You should have come to me as your friend.

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:17.140
Yes, I know the laws as surely as I know

00:40:17.140 --> 00:40:18.880
that I would break them without a moment's hesitation

00:40:18.880 --> 00:40:20.300
if your son came to me.

00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:22.860
I stood behind you when the rest of this town blamed you

00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:25.320
for Colin Hart's death because I believed in your judgment.

00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:27.700
I told my sister that you were a decent man,

00:40:27.820 --> 00:40:28.780
worthy of her heart.

00:40:29.100 --> 00:40:29.980
I may not have...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:34.220
have liked you, but I always respected what you were.

00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:37.800
I admired the doctor enough that I could forgive the man.

00:40:37.980 --> 00:40:39.580
Well, not anymore.

00:40:39.600 --> 00:40:40.660
I am through with you.

00:40:41.330 --> 00:40:43.330
From this day forth, you stay away from my family,

00:40:43.430 --> 00:40:44.970
keep out of their lives, and you'd best

00:40:44.970 --> 00:40:46.110
keep your distance from me.

00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:50.930
And if I don't make myself clear, I encourage you to test me.

00:41:01.850 --> 00:41:02.250
Hey, Hugh.

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:05.980
Hey, I was picking up a little food.

00:41:06.080 --> 00:41:06.980
You going for a walk?

00:41:07.890 --> 00:41:09.490
Yeah, I was at the bookstore looking at books.

00:41:10.360 --> 00:41:12.180
Pretty much the same stuff there was last week.

00:41:12.840 --> 00:41:13.580
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:41:13.640 --> 00:41:15.920
That copy of Seabiscuit's been in the window since I moved here.

00:41:16.390 --> 00:41:18.550
I'm thinking about buying it just to see whatever they put up next.

00:41:20.220 --> 00:41:20.900
And you want to ride home?

00:41:21.060 --> 00:41:21.620
I got my car.

00:41:23.370 --> 00:41:24.230
Actually, you want to walk?

00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:26.360
I kind of feel like walking for a little bit.

00:41:26.740 --> 00:41:27.200
Where are we going?

00:41:28.730 --> 00:41:29.010
Nowhere.

00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:29.960
Sorry.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.260
Sounds good.

00:41:30.520 --> 00:41:33.970
So how are things at home?

00:41:34.460 --> 00:41:35.160
Getting any better?

00:41:36.440 --> 00:41:36.740
A little.

00:41:37.830 --> 00:41:40.670
School, on the other hand, is going to be a torture zone until we graduate.

00:41:41.090 --> 00:41:43.590
In fact, I'll give you a dollar to sit with me at lunch.

00:41:44.160 --> 00:41:44.460
Deal.

00:41:45.560 --> 00:41:46.560
Supposed to say it's free.

00:41:46.860 --> 00:41:48.460
I know an opportunity when I see one.

00:41:52.810 --> 00:41:53.270
You're sad.

00:41:54.770 --> 00:41:54.990
A little.

00:41:55.490 --> 00:41:56.170
Something happened.

00:42:00.440 --> 00:42:01.420
Madison and I broke up.

00:42:03.050 --> 00:42:03.810
What? When?

00:42:04.650 --> 00:42:05.610
About an hour ago.

00:42:07.130 --> 00:42:07.670
Oh, my God.

00:42:07.850 --> 00:42:09.770
The other day, you said that everything was fine, I thought.

00:42:09.930 --> 00:42:11.910
Yeah, yeah, no, I lied a little bit.

00:42:12.580 --> 00:42:13.400
Don't ask me why.

00:42:15.430 --> 00:42:15.630
Why?

00:42:17.490 --> 00:42:17.970
I don't know.

00:42:18.210 --> 00:42:21.670
I guess I thought that if I pretended everything was great, it would actually be great.

00:42:23.310 --> 00:42:23.950
Projecting hope?

00:42:24.570 --> 00:42:25.530
It worked for Seabiscuit.

00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:29.460
I'm sorry.

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:31.640
Yeah, me too.

00:42:33.670 --> 00:42:36.310
I know that you liked her, and she seemed really great, but...

00:42:37.260 --> 00:42:37.640
But what?

00:42:39.160 --> 00:42:42.900
But if she was dumb enough to let you go, she mustn't have been that perfect.

00:42:44.130 --> 00:42:46.910
She's gonna be really upset when she realizes what she gave up, trust me.

00:42:49.730 --> 00:42:51.650
Yeah, I say we keep walking until we run out of fries.

00:42:51.910 --> 00:42:53.150
We can always buy more fries.

00:42:57.330 --> 00:42:59.770
Walk through the town to Central.

00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:05.680
Catching my breath, now I picture you across the street
